er/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-05-01T12:26:54Z","updated_at":"2021-05-01T12:26:54Z","body":"Maybe I'm confused by the meaning of a `groupSetting` but my understanding was that calling `getAsGroups` here is legitimate assuming the setting is valid as a group setting. For instance the `monitor.jvm.gc.collector` group setting behaves similarly: setting `monitor.jvm.gc.collector.nonsense: foo` passes validation and then fails when initialising the `JvmGcMonitorService` for much the same reason:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[2021-05-01T13:13:16,763][ERROR][o.e.b.ElasticsearchUncaughtExceptionHandler] [MacBook-Pro.lan] uncaught exception in thread [main]\r\norg.elasticsearch.bootstrap.StartupException: SettingsException[Failed to get setting group for [] setting prefix and setting [nonsense] because of a missing '.']\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.bootstrap.Elasticsearch.init(Elasticsearch.java:163) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.bootstrap.Elasticsearch.execute(Elasticsearch.java:150) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.cli.EnvironmentAwareCommand.execute(EnvironmentAwareCommand.java:75) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.cli.Command.mainWithoutErrorHandling(Command.java:116) ~[elasticsearch-cli-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.cli.Command.main(Command.java:79) ~[elasticsearch-cli-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.bootstrap.Elasticsearch.main(Elasticsearch.java:115) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.bootstrap.Elasticsearch.main(Elasticsearch.java:81) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\nCaused by: org.elasticsearch.common.settings.SettingsException: Failed to get setting group for [] setting prefix and setting [nonsense] because of a missing '.'\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.common.settings.Settings.getGroupsInternal(Settings.java:440) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.common.settings.Settings.getAsGroups(Settings.java:452) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.monitor.jvm.JvmGcMonitorService.<init>(JvmGcMonitorService.java:105) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.monitor.MonitorService.<init>(MonitorService.java:32) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.node.Node.<init>(Node.java:423) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.node.Node.<init>(Node.java:278) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.bootstrap.Bootstrap$5.<init>(Bootstrap.java:217) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.bootstrap.Bootstrap.setup(Bootstrap.java:217) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.bootstrap.Bootstrap.init(Bootstrap.java:397) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\tat org.elasticsearch.bootstrap.Elasticsearch.init(Elasticsearch.java:159) ~[elasticsearch-7.12.0.jar:7.12.0]\r\n\t... 6 more\r\n```\r\n\r\n(The consequences aren't so severe here since the setting is static and can be fixed).\r\n\r\nMy reasoning was that the only two group settings I tested had the same issue, so this seemed to be something infrastructural rather than us using the setting wrongly in the decider. It could just be the same bug in both places.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/830624829/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"DaveCTurner","id":5058284,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNTgyODQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5058284?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTurner","html_url":"https://github.com/DaveCTurner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaveCTu